{
  "description": "Search quality test set: realistic queries ixnos-data must answer well, with relevance criteria instead of hand-picked results so it stays valid as data grows. A record is relevant to a query when it satisfies every criterion given (any_cpv_prefix: one of its CPV codes starts with one of these; title_any: its normalised title contains one of these normalised stems; organisation_any: its organisation name contains one of these; nuts_prefix: its NUTS code starts with this; reference: exact ΑΔΑΜ/ΑΔΑ; organisation_vat: exact VAT). Metrics: precision@10 and recall@10 against the relevant set, per category. Criteria checked against six months of real results (September 2026). Scored with `python -m ixnos_data_pipeline.search_quality --api <url>`, which fails when a category's precision@10 drops below its threshold.",
  "categories": {
    "trade": "What a small business sells, in plain Greek",
